speechtext:
Just this further word;
I appreciate the position the minister is taking, and he is being perfectly logical so far as the administration of the Unemployment Insurance Act is concerned. But I want to say that the man who has lost his employment at a fairly good wage rate and is forced to take employment at a lower wage rate does not regard it as the last, word in justice merely to get his unemployment insurance, which is a lower rate still. He wants another job at a rate somewhat comparable with that which he had during the war. My concern with this memorandum is not so much that it is vitiating the Unemployment Insurance Act as that trade unionists feel that it has a depressing effect on the wage level generally.

Unemployment Insurance
